{"name":"Calm Iridescence","hex":"#dee2eb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"calm","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Peaceful, quiet, especially free from anger and anxiety.","Free of noise and disturbance."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The state of being calm; peacefulness; absence of worry, anger, fear or other strong negative emotion.","The state of being calm; absence of noise and disturbance."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/calm"},{"term":"iridescence","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The condition or state of being iridescent; exhibition of colors like those of the rainbow; a prismatic play of color.","Any shimmer of glittering and changeable colors."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/iridescence"}],"entries":[{"title":"Iridescence","blocks":[{"text":"Iridescence is the phenomenon of certain surfaces that appear gradually to change colour as the angle of view or the angle of illumination changes. Iridescence is caused by wave interference of light in microstructures or thin films. Examples of iridescence include soap bubbles, feathers, butterfly wings and seashell nacre, and the mineraloid opal. Pearlescence is a related effect where some or most of the reflected light is white. The term pearlescent is used to describe certain paint finishes, usually in the automotive industry, which actually produce iridescent effects."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Soap_Bubble_-_foliage_background_-_iridescent_colours_-_Traquair_040801.jpg/330px-Soap_Bubble_-_foliage_background_-_iridescent_colours_-_Traquair_040801.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iridescence","wikidata":"Q957208"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Dieselrainbow.jpg/500px-Dieselrainbow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Dieselrainbow.jpg/500px-Dieselrainbow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fuel on top of water creates a thin film, which interferes with the light, producing different colours. The different bands represent different thicknesses in the film. This phenomenon is known as thin-film interference. ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADieselrainbow.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Iridescent_biofilm_on_a_fishtank.JPG/500px-Iridescent_biofilm_on_a_fishtank.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Iridescent_biofilm_on_a_fishtank.JPG/500px-Iridescent_biofilm_on_a_fishtank.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An iridescent biofilm on the surface of a fish tank diffracts the reflected light, displaying the entire spectrum of colours. Red is seen from longer angles of incidence than blue.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIridescent_biofilm_on_a_fishtank.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Black_pearl_and_his_shell.jpg/500px-Black_pearl_and_his_shell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Black_pearl_and_his_shell.jpg/1280px-Black_pearl_and_his_shell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Black_pearl_and_his_shell.jpg/500px-Black_pearl_and_his_shell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The pearlescent shell of a black-lip pearl oyster","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlack_pearl_and_his_shell.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Iride